  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"Every game has a component checklist and labeled storage bags; checking happens before the box returns to the collection.\", \"decision\": \"How should game components be checked after play?\", \"goal\": \"Help guests find compatible games, understand how to play, and enjoy the evening without avoidable waiting or confusion.\", \"problem\": \"A community room is hosting an evening of board games for adults with different levels of experience. Several tables, a host, willing game teachers, short waiting activities, and a varied collection are available. Guests can decline any game and join a later one. Every game has an agreed latest stopping time before the room closes, and ordinary refreshments and conversation have their own small areas.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nOne player reads the component checklist while the others gather and count the pieces into labeled bags. A shared sequence coordinates the cleanup and lets the reader confirm that no listed group was overlooked.\nPlayers divide the component checklist and count their assigned pieces before placing them in the labeled bags. Several small checks proceed together while every part of the game has a clearly responsible person.\nPlayers sort components into labeled bags first, and the teacher checks each bag against the component checklist. The final verification follows organized piles, making shortages easier to locate before the box leaves the table."
    }
  ],
